translate this code from Groovy to python:
```groovy
def minDistance(String word1, String word2) {
    int m = word1.length()
    int n = word2.length()
    int[][] dp = new int[m+1][n+1]

    for (int i = 0; i <= m; i++) {
        dp[i][0] = i
    }

    for (int j = 0; j <= n; j++) {
        dp[0][j] = j
    }

    for (int i = 1; i <= m; i++) {
        for (int j = 1; j <= n; j++) {
            if (word1[i-1] == word2[j-1]) {
                dp[i][j] = dp[i-1][j-1]
            } else {
                dp[i][j] = 1 + Math.min(dp[i-1][j], dp[i][j-1])
            }
        }
    }

    return dp[m][n]
}
```

